# latest_sampling -- leg B.
#
# `latest(RelAtom)` in an EDGE body is the sampled read: the wrapped atom reads
# the current base table and never becomes a trigger, which is exactly
# withLatestFrom's asymmetry. `tick_event` is the trigger; `config` is sampled.
#
# The empty-source case is part of the test: a trigger arriving before `config`
# has any row joins against nothing and derives nothing, which is also what
# withLatestFrom does before its other source has emitted. Neither side has to
# be told to behave that way; it falls out of a join against an empty relation
# on one side and of withLatestFrom's own contract on the other.

rel tick_event(event_id: text) log keep(all).
rel config_change(slot: text, value: text) log keep(all).
rel config(slot: text, value: text) key(1).
rel sampled(event_id: text, value: text) log keep(all).

config(Slot, Value) <+ config_change(Slot, Value).
sampled(EventId, Value) <+ tick_event(EventId), latest(config(_Slot, Value)).
